{"study_accession":"PRJNA797780","secondary_study_accession":"SRP355262","title":"Single-cell transcriptomic analysis of blood T cells from healthy controls, MS patients and COVID-19 patients by 10X genomics","description":"In order to better understand the functional properties of this type of cells under different circumstances, we integrated the single-cell RNA-seq data of peripheral blood CD8+ T cells from healthy subjects, MS patients and COVID-19 patients generated from the 10X Genomics platform using the Seurat package. KIR+CD8+ T cells from different conditions (healthy, MS, and COVID-19) formed a distinct cluster with high expression of effector genes (GZMB and PRF1) as well as KIR transcripts. These findings reveal the commonality of KIR+CD8+ T cells across physiological and diseased status as well as their uniqueness relative to other CD8+ T cells. Overall design: Pan T cells were isolated from the blood of healthy subjects (N=4) and MS patients (N=6) and then subjected to scRNA-seq analysis by 10X genomics. 10X scRNA-seq data of blood CD8 T cells from COVID-19 patients (N=25) were acquired from ArrayExpress: E-MTAB-9357.","pubmed":"35258337","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN25037740","study_accession":"PRJNA797780","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"HC14","description":"HC14","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5820733","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":8,"first_public":"2022-03-10","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_type","pan T cells"],["disease","healthy control"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR17635355","experiment_accession":"SRX13803711","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":28357114,"base_count":8563848428,"first_public":"2022-03-10","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM5820733: HC14 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR17635356","experiment_accession":"SRX13803711","library_layout":"PAI